# Files that are executed inside a Linux container must be checked out with LF
# endings regardless of the developer's platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. A CRLF checkout on Windows turns the shebang `#!/bin/sh`
# into `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the container then fails to start with "exec format
# error" or "bad interpreter" — an error that points nowhere near line endings.
# The image built on a Linux host would work, so it would look like a
# Windows-only mystery.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf

# Generated migration SQL is applied by the database, not by a shell, but keeping
# it stable across platforms avoids spurious diffs.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Never line-ending-convert binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
